//characteristics of virtualization 
| Characteristic | What it Does                                   | Benefit                                   |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Security       | Controls VM execution transparently            | Prevents attacks, safe environment        |
| Sharing        | Multiple VMs on same server                    | Efficient use of resources                |
| Aggregation    | Combine multiple servers into one virtual host | Powerful virtual machine for guests       |
| Emulation      | Create environment different from host         | Run software needing specific OS/hardware |
| Isolation      | VMs separated from each other and host         | Stability and safety                      |


//execution virtualisation 
Definition: Techniques that create a virtual execution environment separate from the physical host.
Purpose: Allows programs (guests) to run as if they are on their own independent machine, even though they share the host hardware.
Key idea: The virtual environment emulates CPU, memory, and I/O, making the guest think it has its own dedicated system.

