OS-level virtualization = efficient, lightweight isolation for applications, all running on the same OS kernel without a hypervisor.

  //running multiple isolated apps on the same OS without needing a separate OS for each.that is the host os 
  OS Virtualization allows multiple isolated environments (like mini-computers) to run on a single operating system kernel 
  — without installing a separate OS for each.

These environments are called containers or OS-level virtual machines.